## Final architecture

Firebase Authentication

Verifies the member or pastor requesting the meeting.

Pastor's personal Google Calendar

Creates the event using the assigned pastor's own OAuth authorization.

Firestore appointment

Stores one Meet URL, one event ID, and the actual host's identity.

Pastor

Actual creator

Opens saved URL and admits member.

Member

Uninvited guest

Opens the same URL and requests admission.

The biggest correction is that the assigned pastor's Google account now creates the event. The pastor isn't just an attendee marked as an organizer, and the member no longer receives a Calendar invitation that could bypass admission.

One integration detail remains to verify in your actual project: whether your existing consultation records are stored in `appointments` or `consultations`, and whether your Express API is already mounted at `/api`. The implementation above makes the collection configurable, but the route and imports must match your existing backend.